Builder 3's 15 math revisions are merged and pushed. The repo check passes, with the same 3 warnings about disputed claims already on the board. QA passed for all 15. The builder only looked at screenshots for 6 of them, so the next review round will catch any visual issues.

The builder disagreed with two findings:
- **exterior-turns:** the review said the reveal unlocked too early. The builder showed that every step is visited, but still made the reveal quote only the sides the learner actually tried.
- **circle-slices-to-rectangle:** the "fan" shape the reviewer saw was a frame caught mid-animation, so the builder left it alone.

Next round, just started:
- **Builder 4:** 15 chemistry revisions. This time it must look at the screenshot sheet for every lesson it changes, not a sample.
- **Fact-check pass 11:** about 45 claims that revision builders reworded.

Wave C so far: 28 lessons revised, about 205 still to go.

Still running:
- builder 2, on the CS revisions;
- the platform engineer's full verify run;
- the R&D lead's review of the knot library's evaluator;
- the accessibility audit of the 49 newer lessons;
- review batch 10.

Three decisions are still waiting on you:
- the 15 held lessons (lift the holds, or give the release manager permission to edit the holds file);
- the 18 lessons that failed accessibility (F-14);
- the usage budget (F-02).

Builder 2's 15 computer-science revisions are merged and pushed. The repo check passes, with the same 3 known warnings about disputed claims. Wave C has now revised 43 lessons.

QA passed on all 15. The builder only looked at 3 of the 15 screenshot sheets directly, so re-review will catch visual problems in the rest.

The builder's judgement calls:
- **cheapest-is-not-shortest:** kept the cost question and declined the reviewer's suggestion. A question about the procedure would have been answerable just by reading the smallest label. It now defines its terms, and adds a moment where a later route costs more.
- **connect-the-towns-cheaply:** the costs changed so the cheap cable actually closes a loop. The tempting wrong answer is now one of the options.

The builder also exposed a limit in our QA test. QA presses each control once, in order. So a lesson can't require an optional step, such as the carry in binary-numbers, before showing its reveal; the test would never get there. Lessons have to route around this. I put it on the board for the evaluation steward (W-152). Making QA follow a scripted path for each lesson would be a constitutional amendment.

Builder 5 has started on the next 15 physics revisions.

Still running:
- builder 4 on chemistry;
- fact-check pass 11;
- the platform engineer's full verify run;
- Bram's review of the knot library's evaluator;
- review batch 10;
- Kiri's fix for the kit's contrast colours.

You are a demo builder in System 3 Company. This is board W-155. After the visual designer's kit token fix (K1 and K6, now merged: text-safe --good/--warn/--bad in the light theme, plus new --good-fill/--warn-fill/--bad-fill for fills), 18 published lessons still fail colour contrast because of colours in their own code. Read CLAUDE.md, company/roles/demo-builder.md, company/design/system.md (the token table) and company/reviews/_accessibility/2026-10-13-published-audit.md, both batches. Each lesson's findings are in company/reviews/<slug>/2026-10-1[34]-accessibility.md. Work in your worktree and commit there (don't push). Never use pkill: use tools/serve.sh.

1. Find the 18 lessons: the 26 failures listed in the audit, minus the 8 now passing (clicks-not-value, lopsided-tree, overfitting, small-hospital-big-swings, supply-demand, water-follows-the-crowd, jackpot-once-a-week, say-seventy-mean-it).
2. In each one, fix the failing text colours:
   - use text-safe tokens (`--good`, `--warn`, `--bad`, `--fg`, `--muted`) for text;
   - use the *-fill tokens only for fills and shapes;
   - replace hard-coded pastels used as text;
   - fix white text on mid-green fills, e.g. use dark text or a darker fill;
   - never use `--domain` as body text on a light card;
   - keep the meaning, and never rely on colour alone.
   Change no pedagogy and no claims. A colour-only fix needs no version bump, but say so in a build.md note.
3. Re-run `node tools/a11y-scan.mjs` on the 18 against a build of your worktree (`NEXT_DIST_DIR=.next-c18 npx next build`, then `git checkout tsconfig.json`, then `tools/serve.sh start 3441 .next-c18`; stop the server afterwards). Then run lesson QA on all 18 (`QA_ONLY`; the feed-chips failures are known, W-136) and `npm run check`.
Report in under 150 words: the commit hash, and pass/fail per lesson after the fix.

You are the release manager of System 3 Company. In Wave A2 you held 15 lessons because `company publish` refused them for lacking a computer-use QA record. Rosa filed QA records for all 15 on 2026-10-14 (company/reviews/<slug>/2026-10-14-qa.md). The 15 are: chain-of-blame, flip-twenty-percent, keep-the-top-85, noisy-compass, twins-never-split, which-question-splits, helium-leaks-first, pencil-lead-vs-diamond, every-message-is-possible, four-words-beat-eight-letters, hamming-points-at-the-bug, in-order-is-sorted, three-pizzas-four-people, red-apple-green-light and stop-when-it-looks-significant. These are your own holds and their reason may now be resolved, so deciding them is your call. Repo: /home/user/system-3-company (work in place, do NOT commit).

For each lesson, confirm that:
- the QA record covers the current lesson code (Demo.tsx unchanged since the QA run; check with git log);
- the latest learner review is launch for the current version;
- every claim is verified.

Remove the hold only for those that pass, then publish them with `node tools/publish-ready.mjs --publish`. Keep the hold, with an updated reason, for any that don't. If your permissions block the edit, stop and say so. Append a "Wave A2 holds resolved" section to company/rituals/records/2026-10-14-launch-review-wave-C.md. Run `npm run check`. Report in under 80 words: the published count before and after, and any holds kept.

Fact-check pass 18 in System 3 Company. Repo: /home/user/system-3-company (work in place, do NOT commit, do NOT touch board.json). Read CLAUDE.md and company/roles/fact-checker.md. Verify every claim still marked "unverified" in src/demos/*/*/meta.json. Most come from wave C:
- builder 10 (15 life-science lessons; new claims potassium-battery c7 and protein-search-space c7);
- builder 11 (15 economics and probability lessons);
- builder 12 (one-recipe-for-sixty, hanoi-tower-doubles, median-without-sorting with 101 bars and seed 38, back-button-stack c5, and dilute-until-none-left c7).
Skip half-of-humanity c1 and continental-jigsaw c1, which need a human. Do not re-check claims already marked disputed (a builder is fixing those). Use derivation, your own node simulation, or a source. Read each Demo.tsx so the stage and the claim agree. Add a "## Pass 18" table to company/reviews/<slug>/2026-10-14-fact-check.md. Run `npm run check`. Report in under 120 words.

